        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philippians 1:21",
        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "But if I live in the flesh, this is the fruit of my labour: yet what I shall choose I wot not.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "GR know."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philippians 1:22",
        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "For I am in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with Christ; which is far better:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "GR hard-pressed to choose."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philippians 1:23",
        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Nevertheless to abide in the flesh is more needful for you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "3 Ne. 28:9 (1–12); D&C 7:5 (1–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philippians 1:24",
        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And having this confidence, I know that I shall abide and continue with you all for your furtherance and joy of faith;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philippians 1:25",
        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "That your rejoicing may be more abundant in Jesus Christ for me by my coming to you again.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philippians 1:26",
        "book": "Philippians",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Only let your conversation be as it becometh the gospel of Christ: that whether I come and see you, or else be absent, I may hear of your affairs, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 165,
            "text": "Philip. 4:1 (1–7)."
          },
          {
            "start": 186,
